<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74367" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξῠρεγμ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, (fr.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀξ-ερυγμία,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρευγμός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the sour fumes caused by indigestion, heartburn,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.344
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				9.43
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>the peevishness</i> or <i>fretfulness</i> caused thereby,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				473
			</span></i> ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρομμυοξυρεγμία,
			ὀξωρεγμία.</span></div>
